From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 18:15:26 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: tas2764: Take the SN012776 brownout and DC blocker
 setup from the DT

The driver wrote a brownout prevention block typed in from a trace to
every SN012776, and left the DC blockers at their reset values. The
Mac's ADT carries both for each amp group (bop-config and
amp-dcblocker-config), and the boot loader now copies them to every
amp's node as apple,bop-config and apple,amp-dcblocker-config.

Program BOP_CFG0..BOP_CFG24 from apple,bop-config, and DC_BLK0 and
DC_BLK1 from the first two bytes of apple,amp-dcblocker-config (the
rest is padding), and drop the copy in the driver. PVDD stays the
brownout source on every SN012776, as before. Without a property its
registers keep their reset values; a property of the wrong length is
a broken device tree and fails the probe.

KUnit tas2764-bop (8 cases): each block is the property byte for byte,
absent means none, a wrong length fails, a TAS2764 ignores both.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
(cherry picked from commit aca03d5c075873218e3be77881662f7db83ce218)
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
